course: dictionary
lesson: 7356
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Playlist is one of them. It can mean a list of songs or videos you choose to play one after another, on a phone, a music app or the radio.
explain: The clues are in the words around it. «Make a playlist» tells you that you are choosing songs yourself. On the radio, a playlist is the list a station has picked to play often, so the clue is the station.
explain: Here is a sentence with a harder word: «The app's "made for you" playlist is not mind reading: an algorithm, a set of rules a computer follows, looks at what you play, skip and like.» The sentence explains algorithm for you, so you can read on without stopping.
fact: A playlist is a list of songs or videos played one after another.
fact: On the radio, a playlist is the list of songs a station has chosen to play often.
fact: Phrases to know: «make a playlist», «add to the playlist» and «shuffle the playlist».
fact: Order matters in a playlist: shuffling changes the order the songs play in.
fact: An algorithm is a set of rules a computer follows.
exercise: Ella makes a playlist for her car journey. What is a playlist? | A kind of car seat | *A list of songs or videos to play one after another | A map of the roads she will drive | A phone with a cracked screen
exercise: «The app's "made for you" playlist is not mind reading: an algorithm, a set of rules a computer follows, looks at what you play.» In this sentence, what is an algorithm? | A song that everyone likes | *A set of rules a computer follows | A playlist made by hand | A person who mixes music at parties
exercise: In computing, a playlist is an example of a list where order matters. Which of these can you do to a playlist? | Paint the songs a new colour | *Add, remove or shuffle songs | Whisper the songs to a friend | Cook the songs in a pan
test: A playlist has three songs lasting 3 minutes, 4 minutes and 5 minutes. How long does it last in total? | 9 minutes | *12 minutes | 3 minutes | 13 minutes
test: Dad says the radio station's playlist is the songs it plays often. What does playlist mean here? | A list of radio presenters | A set of hit songs sung live in the studio | A tape of old speeches | *The songs a radio station has chosen to play often
exam: «A playlist made only from your old habits rarely brings you something truly new.» What does the sentence suggest? | Playlists cannot be changed once they are made | Playlists always bring you brand new songs | Old habits are always bad for music | *If you only pick songs you already know, you rarely find new music
